      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're not alone in feeling like a ghost in a hollow play; it’s a common sense of alienation that therapy can help untangle. Think of it as a deep, quiet rebellion against the shallow surface of life—your perspective is a way to see the cracks and find meaning where others see only the stage. It’s not a medical fix but a personal reclamation of your place in the world, and you can choose to step out of the play or write your own script.",
      "source": "target",
